                <pb facs="0349" n="283" sameAs="frus:frus1934v05/pg283"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.1431/52: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Guatemala</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Hanna</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Guatemala</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1934-07-18T10:00:00-06:00">July 18, 1934—10
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received 12:15 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>47. Department’s 24, July 17, 8 p.m., concerning trade agreement with Government
                    of Guatemala. I judge from recent conversations with the Minister of Foreign
                    Affairs of Guatemala that it would now be agreeable to this Government to begin
                    exploratory conversations for a reciprocal trade agreement.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hanna</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
